"answer": "To measure hormone levels, laboratory tests can be performed on blood, urine, or saliva samples [MLP-1499]. Regarding your second question, yes, people who had mild COVID-19 can develop long-term symptoms known as post-COVID conditions or long COVID [MLP-7807]. These symptoms, which may include fatigue, can linger for weeks, months, or even years regardless of the initial severity of the illness [MLP-7807]."
